                                    <h1>Google Ads Cost for eCommerce Brands 2026-2027 (India + Global)</h1>
                                    <p>Google Ads (Search + Shopping + Performance Max) is the second-largest paid channel for most eCommerce brands after Meta. Costs vary sharply by category, format, and region. Here are current 2026-2027 benchmarks from the eCommerce accounts we operate.</p>
                                    <h2>Google Search CPC by Industry (India 2026)</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Fashion:</strong> ₹8-25.<br><strong>Beauty:</strong> ₹10-35.<br><strong>Jewelry:</strong> ₹18-65 (highest — high-intent + high-AOV).<br><strong>Home &amp; furniture:</strong> ₹15-45.<br><strong>F&amp;B:</strong> ₹6-22.<br><strong>Wellness / supplements:</strong> ₹12-40.<br><strong>Consumer electronics:</strong> ₹10-32.<br><strong>Kidswear:</strong> ₹8-24.</p>
                                    <h2>Google Search CPC by Region</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> ₹6-65 depending on industry.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> AED 1.5-14.<br><strong>USA:</strong> $1.20-9.<br><strong>UK:</strong> £0.90-6.50.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> AUD 1.30-8.</p>
                                    <h2>Google Shopping Performance Benchmarks</h2>
                                    <p>Shopping typically 25-45% lower CPC than Search for equivalent intent. Shopping ROAS 2-6x for growth-stage eCommerce (higher than Search on product-focused searches).</p>
                                    <h2>Performance Max (PMax) — Where It Wins + Fails</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Wins:</strong> broad prospecting, cross-channel efficiency (uses YouTube + Discover + Shopping + Search inventory), lower CPA at scale.<br><strong>Fails:</strong> transparency (limited placement reporting), brand cannibalization (bids on your brand searches unless excluded), creative fatigue when asset library is thin.<br><strong>Best practice:</strong> exclude brand terms, provide 30+ image + 10+ video assets, use audience signals + first-party data.</p>
                                    <h2>ROAS Benchmarks by Format</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Search (brand keywords):</strong> 8-25x (mostly capturing existing intent).<br><strong>Search (non-brand):</strong> 1.8-4x first-order.<br><strong>Shopping:</strong> 2-6x.<br><strong>PMax:</strong> 2-5x.<br><strong>YouTube (via PMax):</strong> harder to isolate; typically 1.5-3x when properly attributed.</p>
                                    <h2>What Actually Lowers Google Ads Cost</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>Product feed optimisation</strong> — titles, images, GTINs. 20-40% lift in Shopping performance.<br>2. <strong>Landing page speed + relevance</strong> — Quality Score directly affects CPC.<br>3. <strong>Negative keyword hygiene</strong> — regular exclusion of irrelevant queries.<br>4. <strong>First-party data audiences</strong> — customer match + retargeting lifts efficiency 15-30%.<br>5. <strong>Structured bidding strategies</strong> — Target ROAS or Target CPA over manual once you have data.</p>

